        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-01-04T12:01:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, Parse is mostly OP but she still has her limits. It's particularly annoying when Extrasensory Awareness turns up all three cards that are all terrible, because unlike most deck control it doesn't dump one of the cards to the bottom. The best you can do is shuffle and pray the other two don't show up after all.</p><p>In non-Dawn shenangians, I'm reminded of a recent F5 variants vs Ultimate Voss game where he played Forced Deployment three turns in a row... while Sub-Zero Atmosphere was out (meaning it would always get destroyed right after it was played). I managed to always survive the onslaught and throw everyone back into the trash again (and did win in the end), but, ouch.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
