        "created_at": "2018-01-04T16:48:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In non-Dawn shenangians, I'm reminded of a recent F5 variants vs Ultimate Voss game where he played Forced Deployment three turns in a row… while Sub-Zero Atmosphere was out (meaning it would always get destroyed right after it was played). I managed to always survive the onslaught and throw everyone back into the trash again (and did win in the end), but, ouch.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's a damned painful scenario; I had something similar happen with La Capitan–got beaten up at the Start of Turn from the crew that was already out, she pulled out A Motley Crew, followed by Plunder, which destroyed the SubZero Atmosophere.&nbsp; At End of Turn, the crew got another round of attacks off, and I was pretty well finished…</p>",
