      {
        "id": 213061,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-01-04T19:29:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, against Dawn and other villains (like Omitron) that have one card that's just way more awful than anything else they have, I work really hard to get out two \"counterspells\" (as we call them).&nbsp; The double play happens way more often that chance would seem to suggest.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In non-Dawn shenangians, I'm reminded of a recent F5 variants vs Ultimate Voss game where he played Forced Deployment three turns in a row… while Sub-Zero Atmosphere was out (meaning it would always get destroyed right after it was played).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Wait, why would that happen?&nbsp; Forced Deployment goes off at the start of the turn.&nbsp; Sub-Zero Atmosphere doesn't do anything to cards that go off at the start, only ones that go off at the end.&nbsp; That should only happen if there's an environment that plays villain cards (like Slamara).</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:43:57.036Z",
